Overview
This project is an Excel VBA automation that removes specified values from a specific header/column across selected worksheets.
The macro is controlled entirely through a Control worksheet, making the solution reusable without changing the VBA code for each new file.
Core workflow
```text
Control Sheet
     │
     ├── A2 → Separator
     ├── C1 → Header to locate
     ├── C2:C... → Values to remove
     └── E2:E... → Target worksheets
             │
             ▼
       Find header in Row 1
             │
             ▼
       Process only that column
             │
             ▼
       Split cell values
             │
             ▼
       Remove matching values
             │
             ▼
       Rebuild using same separator
             │
             ▼
       Write result back to cell
```
---
What problem does it solve?
In configuration, CPQ, product-data, and Excel-based data-management workflows, cells may contain multiple values in a delimited format.
For example:
```text
1;2;a;3;4;b;5
```
If `a` and `b` need to be removed, manually editing thousands of cells is inefficient and error-prone.
This automation allows the user to maintain a simple control list:
```text
a
b
```
and automatically transform:
```text
1;2;a;3;4;b;5
```
into:
```text
1;2;3;4;5
```
---
Control Sheet Structure
The workbook uses the following control structure:
Cell / Column	Purpose
`A2`	Separator used inside target cells
`C1`	Header name to locate in target worksheets
`C2:C...`	Values that should be removed
`E2:E...`	Worksheets that should be processed
Example
```text
A2 = ;
C1 = Product Values

C2 = a
C3 = b
C4 = xyz;abc

E2 = Sheet1
E3 = Sheet2
E4 = Sheet5
```
The macro interprets the deletion list as:
```text
a
b
xyz
abc
```
---
Example
Before
Suppose `Sheet1` contains:
Product Values	Description	Price
`1;2;a;3;4;b;5`	`a;b`	100
`10;xyz;20`	`hello`	200
`abc;30;40`	`xyz`	300
`a`	`test`	400
Control Sheet:
```text
Separator: ;
Header: Product Values

Values to remove:
a
b
xyz
abc
```
After
Product Values	Description	Price
`1;2;3;4;5`	`a;b`	100
`10;20`	`hello`	200
`30;40`	`xyz`	300
(blank)	`test`	400
Only the column under Product Values is modified.
The `Description` and `Price` columns are untouched.
---
Supported Separators
The separator can be any string supported by VBA's `Split` function.
Examples:
```text
;
```
```text
; 
```
```text
|
```
```text
,
```
```text
||
```
```text
###
```
For example, if:
```text
A2 = ||
```
and a target cell contains:
```text
1||2||a||3||b||4
```
the result becomes:
```text
1||2||3||4
```
---
Key Features
1. Control-sheet driven
No hard-coded deletion list is required.
Users can update the Control sheet and rerun the macro.
2. Header-specific processing
The macro searches Row 1 of each target worksheet for the header specified in `C1`.
Only the column containing that header is processed.
3. Multiple values per control cell
A single Control Column C cell can contain:
```text
xyz;abc;123
```
The macro automatically separates these into individual values.
4. Delimited cell processing
Target cells such as:
```text
A;B;C;D
```
are split, filtered, and rebuilt.
5. Standalone values
A cell containing only:
```text
ABC
```
is also handled if `ABC` is in the removal list.
6. Case-insensitive matching
The macro treats:
```text
ABC
abc
Abc
```
as the same value.
7. Whitespace handling
Leading and trailing spaces are ignored when comparing values.
8. Target worksheet control
Only worksheets listed in Column E are processed.
9. No row or column deletion
The macro does not delete Excel rows or columns.
It only modifies the cell value under the specified header.
10. Missing-sheet and missing-header reporting
The completion message reports worksheets that could not be found and worksheets where the specified header was missing.
---
Dummy File
`Dummy_Control_File.xlsx` is included in this repository.
It contains:
`Control`
`Sheet1`
`Sheet2`
`Sheet5`
The dummy workbook demonstrates the control-sheet configuration and sample data.
> The `.xlsx` file is intentionally provided without embedded VBA. Import `RemoveSpecifiedValues.bas` into the VBA editor of a macro-enabled copy when testing the automation.
