---
Technical Approach
The automation follows a simple data transformation pattern:
```text
Read Control Data
       ↓
Build Removal Dictionary
       ↓
Read Target Worksheets
       ↓
Find C1 Header in Row 1
       ↓
Identify Header Column
       ↓
Read Each Cell Below Header
       ↓
Split by Configured Separator
       ↓
Filter Removal Values
       ↓
Rebuild Delimited String
       ↓
Write Back to Same Cell
```
A VBA `Scripting.Dictionary` is used for fast value lookup.
This avoids repeatedly searching the Control sheet for every target cell.
---
Safety Considerations
The macro is designed to limit unintended changes:
Only worksheets listed in Column E are processed.
Only the column matching `C1` is processed.
The header itself is not modified.
Other columns are not modified.
Rows are not deleted.
Excel columns are not deleted.
Duplicate removal values are automatically ignored.
Missing worksheets are reported.
Missing headers are reported.
Excel calculation, events, and screen updating are restored after execution.
Recommendation
Always test the macro against a copy of the source workbook before processing production data.
